---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import heritagePlazaPhoto from '../../assets/communities/andover/city-of-andover-heritage-plaza-better.jpg';
import amphitheaterAerialPhoto from '../../assets/communities/andover/andover-capitol-federal-amphitheater-city-of-andover.jpg';
import discGolfPhoto from '../../assets/communities/andover/city-of-andover-central-park-disc-golf.jpg';
import andoverDaysPhoto from '../../assets/communities/andover/city-of-andover-heritage-andover-days.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Andover, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A practical introduction to Andover, Kansas, including its location east of Wichita, residential growth, Central Park, and property considerations."
  pageClass="page-interior page-andover"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Andover"
    title="A growing city just east of Wichita."
    intro="Andover is an independent city with close physical connections to the Wichita metro and its own parks, neighborhoods, civic center, and community identity."
    image={heritagePlazaPhoto}
    imageAlt="An aerial view of Heritage Park Plaza in Andover, with its pond, string lights, and open lawn"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center 40%"
    imagePositionMobile="center 35%"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="andover-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p>
        <h2 id="andover-overview-title">A separate city at Wichita's eastern edge.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Andover is an incorporated city in western Butler County, directly east of Wichita. US-54/400, commonly called Kellogg, runs through the city and provides a direct route into east Wichita, while nearby connections to K-96 and I-35 make it relatively easy to reach other parts of the Wichita area.</p>
        <p>One of Andover's biggest draws is how closely it connects to Wichita while still feeling like its own community. That makes it convenient for people who work, shop, or spend time on Wichita's east side, while Andover keeps adding neighborhoods, businesses, and recreation space of its own. Central Park, the Capitol Federal Amphitheater, and the Redbud Trail give it a more developed feel than its size suggests.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="andover-housing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Housing and residential growth</p>
        <h2 id="andover-housing-title">Established neighborhoods and newer development share the map.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Andover includes established residential areas as well as substantial newer development. The City's residential-development page identifies Cornerstone, Prairie Creek, and Heritage Commons among the additions that have helped shape the city's housing map.</p>
        <p>Those names are broad reference points rather than statements about current inventory or available lots. When comparing homes, look at the specific lot, property age, included features, restrictions, and any HOA or special-assessment obligations tied to the address.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="andover-park-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">A local center</p>
          <h2 id="andover-park-title">Capitol Federal Amphitheater anchors Andover Central Park.</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">Central Park is a major civic and recreation area within the city. Beyond the amphitheater, it also holds Lake George, the Redbud Trail, and a free 18-hole disc golf course, making it one of Andover's more versatile public spaces.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-grid reveal-stagger">
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media">
            <Picture
              src={amphitheaterAerialPhoto}
              formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
              sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
              alt="An aerial view of Capitol Federal Amphitheater surrounded by the open lawns, walking paths, and a stream of Andover Central Park"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Capitol Federal Amphitheater</strong>
            <p>Opened in 2018, the amphitheater sits at the center of Central Park and hosts concerts, performances, and other community events throughout the year.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media">
            <Picture
              src={discGolfPhoto}
              formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
              sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
              alt="A disc golf basket beside the pond at Andover Central Park"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Part of a larger park</strong>
            <p>Central Park also includes a free 18-hole disc golf course, along with connections to Lake George and the Redbud Trail, which runs west toward the larger trail system extending into Wichita, with 13th Street Sports Park linked directly to the trail.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="andover-days-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid">
      <div class="photo-story-copy" data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">A yearly tradition</p>
        <h2 id="andover-days-title">Greater Andover Days fills Central Park each fall.</h2>
        <p>Greater Andover Days traces back to 1967, when the festival began as a way to bring the community together. Held annually in early October, it's grown into a three-day event with a parade, carnival, fireworks, live music, a car show, and a business and craft expo, much of it centered at Central Park.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-media" data-reveal="right">
        <div class="photo-story-main">
          <Picture
            src={andoverDaysPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
            alt="A lit carnival ride and midway at dusk during Greater Andover Days"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="photo-story-caption">It's one of the clearest examples of Central Park working as Andover's civic gathering place, worth keeping in mind alongside the amphitheater and trail system when you're weighing a home near the park against one further out.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="andover-practical-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical things to consider</p>
        <h2 id="andover-practical-title">Compare the property and its connections.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>For a particular address, confirm whether the property is inside Andover city limits and which municipal details apply. Then compare its relationship to US-54/400 and the other roads and destinations you expect to use regularly.</p>
        <p>The home's age, lot characteristics, maintenance needs, and development type also deserve attention. In a newer addition, confirm what's included and which property-specific restrictions or costs apply.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="andover-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p>
          <h2 id="andover-search-title">What should you verify when looking in Andover?</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">These questions help connect the broader Andover picture to the details that can vary by address, neighborhood, and property type.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Is this property inside Andover city limits, and which municipal services or requirements apply?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Is the home in an established neighborhood or a newer development?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How does the location relate to US-54/400 and the routes you'd use most often?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">For newer construction, which lot details, included features, HOA obligations, assessments, restrictions, and costs need verification?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">What maintenance considerations come with the age, materials, and type of this particular home?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages">
    <span>Keep exploring</span>
    <a href="/communities/">All communities <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a>
  </nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about a property in Andover?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
